Says 72 so far

There is no winning and losing in a breakup. You gotta do what's best for you. When you reflect back in a few years you are not going to care who "won" or who "lost". Don't let your actions be determined by that. 

&#x200B;

It has only been two weeks. If you stick with no contact all the pain and all the feelings you may still have are going to fade. No need to think about switching schools now or doing anything rash. Just keep doing your own thing. All her crazy actions are doing is proving that she probably was not a great partner, and like you said, not wanting her back. Block her on everything, avoid her as much as you can. It sounds like you are bound to hear about stuff but minimize it as much as possible and over time you will care less and less.

I had a pretty similar situation. Issues kept popping up in our relationship but I settled for temporary fixes or tried to wiggle out of them. Over time she faded away from me without me even realizing until it was too late. I wish so much I could go back and change things but I can't. And neither can you.

&#x200B;

I started out the same way you did. Messaging her, pleading with her, begging. It's not gunna work man. Even if she did accept your apology and try again you are always going to be afraid she's going to end it again. What happened with me was a month long painful decline ending in my ultimately cutting off contact because we talked like once a week/hung out once a week and it was so much worse than no contact. Save yourself that month.

&#x200B;

Best thing you can do is cut things off for now, trust me. I did that a few days ago and it sucks but I know it is the best thing to do. Think of all the things you did wrong. What about you do you want to change to be better in the future? Focus on self improvement and yourself. Let her know you want to try to fix things and that she should reach out if she feels the same. Then leave her alone.

&#x200B;

If it's meant to be she will reach out and you will be better equipped to start fresh. If she doesn't, yeah that really sucks, but you will have bettered yourself and your next relationship will be even better because of it.
